phpz bundles php-src's `gen_stub.php` and `run-tests.php` from PHP `8.6.0`. See `tools/php/README.md` for their versions and update procedure.

# [Skeleton generator]($heading.id('skeleton-generator'))

```sh
php phpz_skel.php --help
php phpz_skel.php --ext my_php_extension
```

Run these commands in the directory containing the downloaded `phpz_skel.php`. The 0.1.0 generator creates `my_php_extension` with phpz 0.1.0 as its dependency.

| Option | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `--ext` | Required extension name. |
| `--dir` | Parent directory of the project to generate. |
| `--phpz` | Package specification for `zig fetch --save=phpz`. A bare name selects a phpz Git branch or tag. |
| `--zig` | Path to the Zig executable. |
| `--with-php-config` | Path to the `php-config` used to locate development headers. |
| `--with-php-build-system` | Generate the integration files described in [Integration with the PHP build system]($link.page('development/php-build-system')). |
| `--onlyunix` / `--onlywindows` | Generate support only for the selected platform. |
| `--force` | Overwrite generated template files in the target directory. |

# [Generate arginfo]($heading.id('generate-arginfo'))

```sh
zig build gen-stub
```

`zig build gen-stub` copies the bundled generator to `build/gen_stub.php` and processes the extension's stub. The first run may download PHP-Parser and needs a writable `build/` directory and download tools.

You can also use the generator in a matching php-src checkout.

```sh
php /path/to/php-src/build/gen_stub.php my_php_extension.stub.php
```

By default, the build compares the stub's content hash with the one in the arginfo header. Regenerate a stale header. To disable the hash check, pass `.check_arginfo = false` to `Phpz.init` in `build.zig` and rebuild. Disabling it neither updates the header nor verifies Zig signatures against the stub.

# [Build and test]($heading.id('build-and-test'))

After generating the project or updating arginfo, follow [Building and loading extensions]($link.page('development/build')) and run [PHPT tests]($link.page('development/testing')).
